User (tester report): 6 folder lists, about 100 folders; "Remove this
button" -> MView hung, the process was ended; at the next start the ini
was overwritten.
- Not reproduced (Wine, 6 lists x 17 folders: removed and saved fine).
  Remove only deletes the entry in memory, then SortFoldersChanged
  saves (SaveSort) and redraws; no loop there.
- The loss is clear from the code: TIniFile.UpdateFile empties the file
  and writes it anew in place; stopped in that moment (or Windows stalls
  on the write: a synced or network folder, a virus scanner) the ini is
  empty or cut short; the next start read it as all defaults and the
  next save wrote them. That it was cut short means the hang was most
  likely inside the write (the redraw comes after it).
- uSafeFile (new, utility): ReadTextFile; WriteTextFileSafely (a .tmp,
  flushed, MoveFileExW REPLACE_EXISTING | WRITE_THROUGH; rename on
  Linux).
- uConfig: OpenIniFile (TMemIniFile from the file's text) and CommitIni
  for every save (Save, SaveSort, SaveFilters, SaveDirectory,
  SaveWindowBounds); IniEndLine written last; Load checks the ini
  (IniTextComplete: [Startup] and [Sort], ends with a line end, the end
  line when the backup has one), keeps MView.ini.bak of a complete one,
  restores a damaged one from it (kept as MView.ini.damaged); TakeIniNote.
- uIniEditor (the settings screen's save) and uMousePage (the mouse
  profile) write through uSafeFile; uMView's first Default.mouse too.
- uMView: the note as a red steady notice in the middle (FlashNotice
  style 3, IniNoteMs 8 s), 1.5 s after the start (PumpDeliveries).
- TestSort: TestSafeFile (7 checks): 118 pass.
- Checked under Wine: normal start (backup made, end line written);
  Remove with 102 folders (saved, no .tmp left); ini cut at a line end
  inside [DirList1] -> restored (102 folders), notice shown, .damaged
  kept; empty ini with backup -> restored; empty without -> defaults.
- Spec 14 and the 1.1 release notes say so.

